  "post": {
    "caption": "Voyager's golden record isn't solid gold. Each Voyager spacecraft launched in 1977 with a 12 inch golden record. The record is copper with a thin layer of gold on it. Eight records were gold plated, and two flew into space. The plating was done in Gardena, California. An aluminum cover protects each one and holds a little uranium that works as a clock. Carl Sagan chaired the committee that picked the contents, which include greetings in 55 languages and Chuck Berry's Johnny B. Goode. An etched message is addressed to the makers of music.",
